No intervening commits touched this method, confirming 88ddbe5 is the sole introduction point.

## Bug-Introducing Commits
BIC: 88ddbe5ac6ac5aa0f18ade50aa376b25546fb058

## Reasoning

**(1) Investigation:** I searched the git history of `ArenaListener.java` for the `lockFoodLevel` logic and `onFoodLevelChange` handler, since the fix commit directly modifies that method. I traced the evolution of the `if (arena.isRunning()) { if (lockFoodLevel) {...} }` block backward through history to find when it was introduced without the `inArena` check.

**(2) The introducing change:** Commit `88ddbe5` ("Lock food level for players in the lobby or spectator area") refactored `onFoodLevelChange`. Before this commit, the code had:
```java
if (!arena.isRunning()) return;
if (!(event.getEntity() instanceof Player) || !arena.inArena((Player) event.getEntity())) return;
if (lockFoodLevel) event.setCancelled(true);
```
This correctly guarded on `arena.inArena(p)`. The refactor removed that guard entirely while restructuring the logic to also lock food level for lobby/spectator players:
```java
if (arena.isRunning()) {
    if (lockFoodLevel) {
        event.setCancelled(true);
    }
} else {
    if (arena.inLobby(p) || arena.inSpec(p)) {
        event.setCancelled(true);
    }
}
```
The `arena.isRunning()` branch dropped the per-player `inArena` check, so once an arena was running and `lockFoodLevel` was true, *every* player on the server (not just arena participants) had their food level changes cancelled.

**(3) Evidence:** `git show 88ddbe5` clearly shows the removal of `!arena.inArena((Player) event.getEntity())` in the diff. The fix commit `fb5db89` re-adds exactly this check (`arena.inArena(p) && lockFoodLevel`), and no other commit between `88ddbe5` and `fb5db89` touched this method (confirmed via `git log --oneline` on the file range), so `88ddbe5` is the sole origin of the bug.

No significant uncertainty here — the fix is a near-exact reversion of the specific line removed in `88ddbe5`.

